  "name": "Ngbaka-Ma'bo chantefables and sanza song (Lobaye)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Music of the Ngbaka-Ma'bo of the Lobaye forest region of Central African Republic, documented in Simha Arom and Geneviève Dournon's 1964-67 recordings and on Arom's 1970 SELAF disc of tales and chantefables: spoken tales are broken by sung refrains that the narrator leads and listeners answer, and a separate song strand is accompanied by the sanza lamellophone. The Congolese lukembi card stands in for the sanza.",
